    "62": "Removing the wrong value \\(50\\) and adding the correct \\(40\\): mean \\(\\mu=\\frac{100(40)-50+40}{100}=39.9\\). The original \\(\\sum x^{2}=100(5.1^{2}+40^{2})=162601\\); corrected \\(\\sum x^{2}=162601-2500+1600=161701\\), so \\(\\sigma^{2}=\\frac{161701}{100}-39.9^{2}=1617.01-1592.01=25\\), giving \\(\\sigma=5\\). Hence \\(10(\\mu+\\sigma)=10(44.9)=449\\).",
    "75": "A subset of \\(\\{1,\\dots,n\\}\\) with no two consecutive elements is counted by the Fibonacci number \\(F_{n+2}\\) (each element is either omitted, or included forcing the next to be omitted). For \\(n=5\\), \\(n(S_5)=F_7=13\\)."
  },
